{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785784547,"nonce":"eDhto5PnjUAJYESJkWubTic+aqQ=","message":"## Root-cause analysis\n\nThe crash is an unhandled EOFError at the merge-confirmation prompt in the\nshazam -M path when the mbox was supplied on stdin.\n\n**Code path.** With `-m-`, the entire mbox is read from stdin during message\nretrieval, leaving stdin at EOF (and, in pipeline use, not a tty at all).\nWhen `-M` (do_merge) is set, the merge branch of the apply path reaches\nsrc/b4/mbox.py:1029:\n\n    input('Press Enter to continue or Ctrl-C to abort')\n\nThe surrounding try only catches KeyboardInterrupt (mbox.py:1030-1032), so\nthe EOFError from input() on an exhausted/non-tty stdin propagates up as a\nraw traceback. In the reporter's b4 0.15.2 the same input() lived at\nmbox.py:499; the code has since moved but is unchanged in behaviour.\n\n**Why -H does not crash.** Only the do_merge branch (mbox.py:1025) has this\nconfirmation prompt; the -H checkout path execs git directly without asking.\n\n**Existing but undiscoverable mitigation.** The global `-n/--no-interactive`\nflag (command.py:316) routes around the prompt via the no_interactive\nparameter (mbox.py:1018,1026), but nothing detects a non-tty stdin to fall\nback to it automatically — in contrast to e.g. get_msgid_from_stdin()\n(src/b4/__init__.py:4175), which does check sys.stdin.isatty().\n\nReported for b4 0.15.2; mechanism verified present in current master.","files":null}]}